#+STATUS: NEXT
#+DEPENDS: xdata:probe:xdsize / xdroom cases (vendor byte counts to MEASURE)
#+BRANCH: fix-xdroom-xdsize
xdroom-xdsize-not-implemented — XDROOM / XDSIZE are still nil stubs
==================================================================

Status: NEXT -- implemented with a provisional byte table, vendor counts
to be measured (was DEFERRED, schms-data-selection 1.6.8). Parent:
drawing-data-structures-parity.

XDROOM (remaining xdata capacity, in bytes, for an entity) and XDSIZE
(the byte size a supplied xdata list would occupy) are registered as M6
nil-returning stubs in autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp
(*m6-stub-names*). The full XData read/write path (regapp + the 1000..1071
codec through entget/entmod) is implemented; only these two size-accounting
queries are missing.

To implement, the model would need a byte-cost function over an xdata
group list (AutoCAD budgets ~16 KB per entity per application) and XDROOM
= budget - used. The in-memory model does not currently bound xdata, so a
faithful XDROOM needs the vendor's per-code byte sizes:
  1000 string: 3 + strlen ; 1001 appname: 3 + strlen ; 1002 brace: 1 ;
  1003 layer: 1+? ; 1004 binary: 1 + nbytes ; 1005 handle: like 1000 ;
  1010/1011/1012/1013 point: 25 ; 1040/1041/1042 real: 9 ;
  1070 int16: 3 ; 1071 int32: 5. Verify the exact table against the
AutoCAD/BricsCAD reference before shipping numbers.

SCHMS does not call XDROOM/XDSIZE (inventory: 0 sites), so this is low
priority; filed so it is not silently skipped.

* Fix (2026-10-22)

XDSIZE and XDROOM are real builtins now (no longer M6 nil stubs):

- autolisp-builtins-core/source/api.lisp: BUILTIN-XDSIZE, BUILTIN-XDROOM,
  XDATA-LIST-BYTE-SIZE, XDATA-GROUP-BYTE-SIZE, +XDATA-BYTE-BUDGET+ (16383,
  from the spec's xdroom example: 16162 free = 221 of 16383 used).
  - (xdsize LST): LST is ((APP pair ...) ...), optionally headed by -3 (so
    (assoc -3 (entget e '("*"))) is accepted). Each APP must be registered
    (checked through HOST-TBLSEARCH "APPID"). Failures signal an AutoLISP
    error AND set ERRNO, per the Error Codes Reference: 48 unknown group
    code / wrong value type, 49 unbalanced 1002 braces, 50 group not
    headed by an application name, unregistered application, or a 1001
    inside an application's pairs. Success sets ERRNO 0.
  - (xdroom ENAME): 16383 minus the XDSIZE of every application's xdata
    on ENAME, read through HOST-ENTGET with the "*" application list (so
    no new host generic: cador answers through its existing ENTGET, the
    nihil host signals host-not-supported as for every drawing access).
    A non-ename is an argument error; an ename that names no live object
    returns nil with ERRNO 2, as ENTGET.
- autolisp-runtime/source/api.lisp: AUTOLISP-RUNTIME-ERROR-ERRNO maps the
  new condition codes :xdata-unrecognized-type / :xdata-improper-nesting /
  :xdata-improper-appid to 48 / 49 / 50 (otherwise the error path would
  overwrite ERRNO with the generic 4).

Byte table used (PROVISIONAL -- one type byte per group + payload; a
string payload = 2-byte length + characters; source: the in-memory/DWG
xdata layout as commonly described, consistent with the costs listed
above, except the brace which is 2 = type byte + 1, not 1):

| group                              | bytes          |
|------------------------------------+----------------|
| application header (APPNAME)       | 3 + len(name)  |
| 1000 string, 1003 layer, 1005 hdl  | 3 + len        |
| 1002 "{" / "}"                     | 2              |
| 1004 binary (hex digits)           | 2 + ceil(n/2)  |
| 1010 / 1011 / 1012 / 1013 point    | 25             |
| 1040 / 1041 / 1042 real            | 9              |
| 1070 int16                         | 3              |
| 1071 int32                         | 5              |
| budget per object                  | 16383          |

Lengths count characters (= bytes for ASCII). Calibration hint: the R12
viewport ACAD xdata (1000 "MVIEW", 2 braces pairs, 9x1070, 2x1010,
13x1040) costs 217 under this table vs the spec example's 221 -- close but
not proven, so the table is NOT final.

To MEASURE (why this stays NEXT): probes/sources/probe-xdata.lsp now runs
CAD-PROBE-RUN-XDSIZE-PROBES (suite "xdsize" / "xdroom"): bare header and
header+1 char, each group code alone (1000 empty/3/10 chars and one
non-ASCII char, brace pair, 1003, 1004 4 bytes, 1005 1 and 2 chars, 1010,
1011, 1040-1042, 1070, 1071), two applications, the documented example,
the three error cases (with ERRNO), and xdroom of a fresh circle / after a
known payload / xdsize of that payload. Run make probe-autocad and
probe-bricscad, then adjust XDATA-GROUP-BYTE-SIZE (and the header cost and
budget) to the measured numbers and update the tests in
autolisp-builtins-core/tests/drawing-data-tests.lisp (dd-xdsize-*,
dd-xdroom-*). Also open: whether XDROOM on a non-graphical object
(dictionary, xrecord) and XDSIZE of an empty list behave as here (0).

Tests: autolisp-builtins-core/tests/drawing-data-tests.lisp
dd-xdsize-sizes-xdata-lists, dd-xdsize-argument-errors,
dd-xdroom-reports-remaining-xdata-room, dd-xdroom-argument-errors,
dd-xdsize-on-the-nihil-host -- red before (nil stubs), green after.
